{
  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) achieved 0.619 acc / 0.610 F1, a ~9-point jump over the best singleprofile multimodal result (config_016, 0.527). This strongly suggests multiprofile aggregation is a critical design axis. However, we have only tested the simplest aggregation (avgpool). Uncertainty: it is unknown whether a transformer-based aggregation can capture inter-profile relationships that simple mean-pooling misses, or whether avgpool is already near-optimal for this task. This experiment (config_020) changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all other settings (pca_n2000, resnet50, concat fusion, multiprofile) constant, making it a clean controlled comparison against config_018. If transformer substantially outperforms avgpool, it identifies aggregation architecture as a high-value axis to further explore; if it performs similarly, it confirms avgpool sufficiency and redirects budget toward other axes (image encoder, RNA encoder). This is the best use of the next experiment because it directly extends the strongest finding with a minimal, interpretable change that reduces uncertainty about a key architectural decision."
}

